    <string name="preview_text">ދިވެހި ސަބްޓައިޓަލް\nމަރުޙަބާ!</string>

    <string name="help_text">OPEN\n• Open a video from your phone or a link, then load an .srt, .vtt, .ass or .ssa file. You can also write subtitles with no video.\n\nWATCH\n• Subtitles show on the video in Thaana. Turn the phone sideways (or tap the full-screen button) for full screen.\n• Out of sync? Use Sync − / Sync + (tap = 0.1 s, hold = 1 s). It is applied when you save.\n\nWRITE\n• + Add creates a line at the current video time.\n• Tap a line to jump to it. Hold a line for edit, split, merge, insert and delete.\n• [ Start and End ] set the selected line\'s times to the current video time — great for timing while you watch.\n• Thaana phonetic typing turns Latin keys into Thaana: h ހ, S ށ, n ނ, r ރ, b ބ, L ޅ, k ކ, w އ, v ވ, m މ, f ފ, d ދ, t ތ, l ލ, g ގ, N ޏ, s ސ, D ޑ, z ޒ, T ޓ, y ޔ, p ޕ, j ޖ, c ޗ; vowels a ަ, A ާ, i ި, I ީ, u ު, U ޫ, e ެ, E ޭ, o ޮ, O ޯ, q ް (sukun).\n\nFIX\n• Shift all timings, find &amp; replace, fix overlaps, undo.\n• Convert ASCII Thaana turns old A_Faruma-style text into real Thaana.\n\nSAVE\n• Save writes back to the file you opened (or asks where). Export WebVTT and Share are in the menu. Your work is also autosaved as a draft.</string>
